        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "A wider aperture admits more light and can produce shallower depth of field. A narrower aperture admits less light and can keep more of the scene in focus. A fast shutter can freeze motion; a slow shutter records motion across time. These are creative decisions as well as exposure decisions."
